# LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree, whatever the
# contributor's core.autocrlf. With autocrlf=true (Git for Windows' default) the
# checkout wrote CRLF, while the tools that rewrite files here — Node scripts
# (sync-version.mjs), cargo, editors — write LF: every such write left a file
# "modified" with an empty diff, which then blocked merges. Binary files are
# still detected and left untouched by text=auto.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Real result files of the game, kept byte for byte: the game writes CRLF and
# tabs, and the test that parses them "as written" must see exactly that.
src-tauri/src/raceresult/samples/*.json -text
